On Wednesday 28 February 2007 23:21, Alex Martini wrote:
> In practical terms, just remember that
> - any word that starts with a vowel must have a full stop before it
> - any cmene must end with a full stop

And one more: any name of a letter which has a cmavo of the form Cy in it is 
followed by a full stop. Otherwise you can't tell {le dy cilta} "D's thread" 
from {ledycilta} "hypha" (fungus-thread).

